######## 

$ kagebunshin project init app
created project app with environment dev

-- under a prefix

$ kagebunshin project add-source app dev --provider aws_sm --prefix team/ --profile acme-dev
added a source to environment dev of project app; it replaces the default source, the local store's section, unless you add `--provider file` too

$ kagebunshin status
daemon: unlocked
providers:
  aws_sm  profile acme-dev  ok
project: app
env: dev
.env.example: none found
1 key
  OPEN  aws_sm:team/open
warning: aws_sm prefix team/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret team/closed, which this login may not read

$ kagebunshin run -- sh -c 'echo open is ${OPEN:+set}, closed is ${CLOSED:-unset}'
kagebunshin: warning: aws_sm prefix team/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret team/closed, which this login may not read
kagebunshin: warning: no .env.example found, so every key the environment has is passed (1 key); `kagebunshin project example` writes one from the keys the code reads, to pass only those
open is set, closed is unset

$ kagebunshin --json run --strict -- true
{"warning":"aws_sm prefix team/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret team/closed, which this login may not read"}
{"warning":"no .env.example found, so every key the environment has is passed (1 key); `kagebunshin project example` writes one from the keys the code reads, to pass only those"}

$ kagebunshin next
project app, environment dev: done. 1 of 1 keys set; `true` ran with them on <day>. They come from aws_sm:team/open (1).
suggested, not needed: this app has no .env.example, so a command run here gets the one key of the environment. One listing the keys the app reads from its environment, one `NAME=` to a line, names only, gives a command those and no more (kagebunshin found none in the code itself).

$ kagebunshin list --keys --prefix team/ --profile acme-dev
2 matches
  team/closed  aws_sm  (keys not read: access to secret team/closed was denied)
  team/open    aws_sm  OPEN

-- named on its own

$ kagebunshin project add-env app only
added environment only to project app

$ kagebunshin project add-source app only --provider aws_sm --secret team/closed --profile acme-dev
added a source to environment only of project app; it replaces the default source, the local store's section, unless you add `--provider file` too

$ kagebunshin --env only run -- true
kagebunshin: cannot resolve environment only of project app: aws_sm secret team/closed (profile acme-dev): access to secret team/closed was denied
hint: ask the human to let profile acme-dev read it (it needs secretsmanager:GetSecretValue on that secret); or, if this project does not need it, take it out: kagebunshin project remove-source app only 1
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin --env only next
the environment cannot be resolved
next (you): cannot resolve environment only of project app: aws_sm secret team/closed (profile acme-dev): access to secret team/closed was denied; ask the human to let profile acme-dev read it (it needs secretsmanager:GetSecretValue on that secret); or, if this project does not need it, take it out: kagebunshin project remove-source app only 1
